{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Scope ruling: this is INFORMATIONAL, not a blocker\n\nOperator ruling received after this ticket was filed: LLMs are non-deterministic, and comparing\ntwo MODELS against one another is out of scope for epic 061c. The epic's scope is that the same\nPAYLOADS reach the LLM and the same TOOLS are available, regardless of model and provider.\nTicket 0d76's acceptance criteria are retargeted accordingly — verdict agreement, decision flips,\nrecall and false-accept are now recorded as INFORMATIONAL evidence, not pass/fail.\n\nSo the claim in this ticket's description that the gold-blind flip criterion \"is now the sole\nremaining blocker on the Bedrock parity slots\" is SUPERSEDED. There is no blocker; the remaining\nfrontier agreement shortfall (0.929) and the three decision flips are the expected outcome of\ncomparing two different models, not a defect.\n\nWhat survives, and is why this ticket is left open rather than withdrawn: the observation about\nthe METRIC itself is independent of the Bedrock decision. `parity_report` computes\n`decision_flips` and `verdict_agreement` symmetrically between the two arms and never consults\nthe gold `label`, even on a gold-labelled corpus where recall and false-accept in the same\nfunction do consult it. Whoever next uses this bar for a genuine A/B of one implementation\nagainst another — the LangGraph -> pydantic-ai cutover it was written for, where both arms ARE\nthe same model — inherits a criterion that cannot tell an improvement from a regression. That is\nthe same class of defect as 62ac, and it is worth deciding deliberately.\n\nNo root-cause investigation of the specific model differences was performed, and none is\nauthorised: that question has been ruled irrelevant."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785724816742781001,"uuid":"73c364b1-bcca-4d88-a228-88f47b60243e"}